                "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                "word": "headroom",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "28e4a560-a770-4aa1-87fe-c28b03ff977a",
                        "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "headrooms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad630a6c-012f-362a-87dc-e62dd768620d",
                        "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The vertical clearance above someone's head, as in a tunnel, doorway etc; room (space) for one's head."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "84993174-0d5e-3b12-b648-fc51f83a53cf",
                        "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The vertical measurement, top to bottom, for example for clearance under a bridge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "023e91dc-8bba-4df3-b2e8-141beef8b7b8",
                                "sense_id": "84993174-0d5e-3b12-b648-fc51f83a53cf",
                                "text": "With a rare and beautiful ease one can now ring up a boffin, as I did the other day, and say: \"As a price for not opposing our Parliamentary Powers for a new marshalling yard, the Council at X demands that the bridge over X Lane shall have 16 ft. 6 in. headroom. This means steepening our gradient from 1 in 70 to 1 in 65 for half a mile on a 20-chain curve. What difference will this make to the loads of Type \"2\", \"3\" and \"4\" diesels please?\". Back comes the answer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46693e37-80d1-4879-8fe2-d1a45165a350",
                                "sense_id": "84993174-0d5e-3b12-b648-fc51f83a53cf",
                                "text": "The new bridge (6) gives headroom of 13ft at high tide, sufficient for present-day river traffic."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "748630f9-2e13-349b-92c0-6b40a8da2a5d",
                        "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The ability of a system to reproduce loud sounds free of distortion; dynamic headroom."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b02c717-e585-44c3-aece-8bc61769a6c7",
                                "sense_id": "748630f9-2e13-349b-92c0-6b40a8da2a5d",
                                "text": "[…] the difference between signal-to-noise ratio and overload reserve (headroom) as well as noise (safety) margin (footroom)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "38083ba3-bd5b-3d8b-ac0f-5db350bf21f2",
                        "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The distance between the actual performance of an algorithm and its maximum possible performance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c043c00-6911-356d-83f0-93d28664130f",
                        "entry_id": "98421eab-c6f7-3c9e-b3e2-276a23c05c12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of headspace (“space between the top of the contents of a container and its seal”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "37653044-1b37-4e36-9d65-0de8257541b0",
                                "sense_id": "9c043c00-6911-356d-83f0-93d28664130f",
                                "text": "For whole pickles and fruit preserves, leave no less than ½ inch of headroom at the top of the jars […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
